    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="ch16">

                <pb facs="0646" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/>

                <head>Status of intergovernmental debts owed the United States by reason of the
                    First World War<anchor n="1" xml:id="ch16-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>[For summary of intergovernmental debts due December 15, 1936, see Department of
                    State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, November 28, 1936, p. 415.
                    For exchanges of correspondence in connection with amounts due the United States
                    under arrangements effected by the World War Foreign Debt Commission, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, as follows: <list>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Belgium:</hi> June 20, 1936, p. 621; December
                            19, 1936, p. 523.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Czechoslovakia:</hi> June 20, 1936, p. 618;
                            December 19, 1936, p. 525.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Estonia:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 589.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Finland:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 583; December 5,
                            1936, p. 458.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">France:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 591; December 5,
                            1936, p. 458; December 19, 1936, p. 512.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Greece:</hi> April 4, 1936, p. 285.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hungary:</hi> June 20, 1936, p. 616; December
                            19, 1936, p. 514.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Italy:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 582; December 19,
                            1936, p. 516.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Latvia:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 593; December 19,
                            1936, p. 517.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Liberia:</hi> February 29, 1936, p. 179.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lithuania:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 584; December
                            19, 1936, p. 519.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Poland:</hi> June 20, 1936, p. 619; December 19,
                            1936, p. 521.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rumania:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 586; December
                            19, 1936, p. 527.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Great Britain</hi>)<hi rendition="#italic">:</hi> June 13, 1936, p.
                            580; December 12, 1936, p. 498.</item>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yugoslavia:</hi> June 13, 1936, p. 588.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The foregoing Department of State Press Releases, omitting the statements of
                    amounts due, are reprinted in <hi rendition="#italic">Annual Report of the
                        Secretary of the Treasury on the State of the Finances for the Fiscal Year
                        Ended June 30, 1936</hi> (Washington, Government Printing Office, 1937), p.
                    288, and <hi rendition="#italic">ibid., 1937</hi> (Washington, Government
                    Printing Office, 1938), p. 271; see also <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.,
                        1936</hi>, p. 77, and <hi rendition="#italic">ibid., 1937</hi>, p. 74.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#ch16-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="ch16-f1-content">
                <p>For previous correspondence, see <ref target="frus1935v01#pg_374">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1935, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 374</ref> ff; concerning the
                    position of the Department of State with respect to the treatment of foreign war
                    debts, see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg567">pp. 567</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
